To retrieve the username from a JWT token in ASP.NET C# WebAPI, follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` package installed in your project. You can install it using NuGet Package Manager.

2. Next, create a method to extract the username from the JWT token. Here's an example:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt;
using System.Security.Claims;
using Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens;

public static string ExtractUsernameFromJwtToken(string jwtToken)
{
    var tokenHandler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
    var key = Encoding.ASCII.Parse("your_secret_key"); // Replace this with your secret key
    var token = tokenHandler.ReadJwtToken(jwtToken, new TokenValidationParameters
    {
        IssuerSigningKey = key,
        ValidateIssuer = false,
        ValidateAudience = false,
        ClockSkew = TimeSpan.Zero
    });

    return token.Claims.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Type == ClaimTypes.Name)?.Value;
}
```

Replace `"your_secret_key"` with your actual secret key used to sign the JWT token.

3. Now, you can use this method to extract the username from a JWT token in your WebAPI controller or service. For example:

```csharp
[HttpGet]
