```
function findMax(arr) {
  let maxValue = arr[0];

  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > maxValue) {
      maxValue = arr[i];
    }
  }

  return maxValue;
}
```

This algorithm takes an array as input and returns the maximum value in that array. It works by iterating through the array and comparing each element with the current maximum value. If an element is greater than the current maximum value, it becomes the new maximum value. Finally, the function returns the maximum value.

